---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SectionLabel from '../../components/editorial/SectionLabel.astro';
import { locations } from '../../data/locations';
---

<Layout title="Locations | Trustora" description="Trustora’s EoR and specialist employment perspective across the European Union, Australia, and the United States." currentPath="/locations/">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="measure page-hero-grid"><div class="page-hero-copy"><SectionLabel>Regional operating context</SectionLabel><h1>Three client corridors. Many local answers.</h1><p>Trustora’s Pakistan entity supports client conversations involving the EU, Australia, and USA—regions with strong technical, scientific, and product ecosystems and distinct employment realities. These are service contexts, not a claim of separate local entities.</p></div><div class="page-hero-note">A region is a starting point. The country and worker facts shape the answer.</div></div></section>
  <section class="section cream-field"><div class="measure"><div class="section-head"><div><SectionLabel>Location index</SectionLabel><h2 class="mt-2">Global in ambition. Local in operation.</h2></div><p>Explore the questions that should enter an EoR conversation before the offer is drafted.</p></div><div class="location-index">{locations.map((location) => <a class="location-row" href={`/locations/${location.slug}/`}><span>{location.number}</span><span><h3>{location.title}</h3><p>{location.short}</p></span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>)}</div></div></section>
  <section class="section dark-field"><div class="measure split-argument"><h2>Country coverage is not the same as country judgment.</h2><div class="prose"><p>Trustora’s point of view is deliberately narrower and more useful: build a strong operating relationship in the corridors where the company has real relationships, then make the next country decision with the right local context.</p><p>Read the <a href="/country-parameters/">country parameters baseline</a>, start with the <a href="/what-is-eor/">EoR model</a>, or <a href="/contact/">bring us the country question</a>.</p></div></div></section>
</Layout>
